The previous version failed only because `Profile::Message` isn't a visible type name; using `auto` for the member pointer fixes that while keeping the same early-exit/branch-hint structure, which helps the compiler lay out the hot path (valid field) fall-through and avoid redundant member reloads.

```cpp
FIT_UINT16 Field::GetNumComponents(void) const
{
    const auto* p = profile;
    if (__builtin_expect(p == NULL, 0))
        return 0;
    const FIT_UINT16 index = profileIndex;
    if (__builtin_expect(index >= p->numFields, 0))
        return 0;
    return p->fields[index].numComponents;
}
```